    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **56 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field derived from the owner's locality/region using the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `timezone` string property to the `OwnerDto` schema (right after `locality`), documenting the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane). The DTO is generated from this spec at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", expression = \"java(deriveTimezone(owner))\")` and a `deriveTimezone(Owner)` default method that computes the region via the existing `deriveLocality(owner)` and maps it through the region-to-timezone table, returning `null` for any region without a known timezone (e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\nDeriving from `deriveLocality` reuses the established region logic (postcode range takes precedence, then city table, then `customerCode`), so `timezone` stays consistent with the `locality` shown on the same response \u2014 matching the test's `REGION_TIMEZONE.get(region(city))` expectation.\n\nThe target test `Cp42Tests` passes, and the entire existing suite remains green.",
